Hypertex Toolkit: The HyperTex Toolkit is a Python software suite for hyperspectral textile data visualization, dataset management, and machine learning. Designed for 224-band Specim FX17 hyperspectral captures, it comprises two core modules: HyperTex UI, a desktop interface for inspecting pixel reflectance spectra, converting LabelMe annotations into 10-channel target maps, and packaging HDF5 datasets; and HyperTex ML, a PyTorch framework implementing Spectral MLP and 3D CNN architectures for pixel-level textile fibre composition regression and inference.

This software is authored by:
Tony Ferreira

This program makes use and is distributed with the following libraries:
* Pytorch: https://pytorch.org/
* TorchVision: https://pypi.org/project/torchvision/
* Numpy: https://numpy.org/
* H5Py: https://www.h5py.org/
* Spectral: https://www.spectralpython.net/
* Matplotlib: https://matplotlib.org/
* OpenCV: https://opencv.org/
* Pilow: https://pypi.org/project/pillow/
* Scikit-learn: https://scikit-learn.org/
* Tkinter: https://docs.python.org/3/library/tkinter.html


